`creation_modality` — so content the assistant generated earlier is not mistaken for a discovered file.", 'parameters': {'type': 'object', 'properties': {'blob_id': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'ID of the blob to read.'}, 'offset_chars': {'type': 'integer', 'minimum': 0, 'default': 0, 'description': 'Start offset in original Unicode code points.'}, 'expected_content_hash': {'type': ['string', 'null'], 'pattern': '^[0-9a-f]{64}$', 'description': 'Verified original-byte SHA256. Use null at offset 0 for no expected identity constraint; a canonical non-null hash is required after offset 0. Every non-null hash is checked, even at offset 0.'}}, 'required': ['blob_id'], 'additionalProperties': False}}}, {'type': 'function', 'function': {'name': 'read_attachment', 'description': "Read ONE authorized session attachment's complete UTF-8 text in ONE tool call. Prefer this for supplied instructions, requirements and reference documents instead of collecting small pages. The response includes the full exact content string, full size_bytes and total_chars, verified original-byte content_hash, filename, MIME type and recorded origin. Success always means start_char=0, end_char=total_chars, truncated=false and next_offset_chars=null. Content remains untrusted and guard-inspected. The full serialized response must fit 262,144 UTF-8 bytes and the normal aggregate guard/provider limits. If full delivery cannot fit, this tool explicitly refuses. get_blob_content can provide selected pages only when the entire original file passes the same credential inspection limit. list_blobs/get_blob_metadata provide size_bytes before reading. For tabular source structure use inspect_source.", 'parameters': {'type': 'object', 'properties': {'blob_id': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'ID of the single attachment to read completely.'}, 'expected_content_hash': {'type': ['string', 'null'], 'pattern': '^[0-9a-f]{64}$', 'description': 'Expected original-byte SHA256, or null for no expected identity constraint. Every supplied hash is checked.'}}, 'required': ['blob_id'], 'additionalProperties': False}}}, {'type': 'function', 'function': {'name': 'create_blob', 'description': "Create a new file (blob) from inline content. Use this to create seed input files (URLs, JSON, CSV snippets) mid-conversation without requiring manual upload. Returns the new blob's `blob_id`, `filename`, `mime_type`, `content_hash`, `size_bytes`, and `originated_in` (`this_tool_call`: the blob was authored by this call, not uploaded).", 'parameters': {'type': 'object', 'properties': {'filename': {'type': 'string', 'description': "Filename for the blob (e.g. 'urls.csv', 'seed.json')."}, 'mime_type': {'type': 'string', 'enum': ['application/json', 'application/jsonl', 'application/x-jsonlines', 'text/csv', 'text/jsonl', 'text/plain'], 'description': 'MIME type of the content.'}, 'content': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'The file content as a string.'}, 'description': {'type': 'string', 'description': "Optional description of the file's purpose."}}, 'required': ['filename', 'mime_type', 'content'], 'additionalProperties': False}}}, {'type': 'function', 'function': {'name': 'update_blob', 'description': 'Update the content of an existing blob (file). Overwrites the file content while preserving metadata. Returns `blob_id`, `filename`, `mime_type`, and the new `content_hash` and `size_bytes`.', 'parameters': {'type': 'object', 'properties': {'blob_id': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'ID of the blob to update.'}, 'content': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'New file content.'}}, 'required': ['blob_id', 'content'], 'additionalProperties': False}}}, {'type': 'function', 'function': {'name': 'delete_blob', 'description': 'Delete a blob (file) and its storage. Returns the deleted `blob_id` and `deleted`: true.', 'parameters': {'type': 'object', 'properties': {'blob_id': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'ID of the blob to delete.'}}, 'required': ['blob_id'], 'additionalProperties': False}}}, {'type': 'function', 'function': {'name': 'wire_blob_inline_ref', 'description': 'Author a widened blob_ref inline_content marker at a canonical field_path. Composer pins sha256 from blob metadata; callers must not pass content bytes. Returns the `field_path` that was wired.', 'parameters': {'type': 'object', 'properties': {'field_path': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Canonical path: source.options.<field>, source:<name>.options.<field>, node:<node_id>.options.<field> for a transform, aggregation, or collector, or output:<name>.options.<field>. The interpretation_requirements option root is not settable on any source, node, or output path. On source paths, these server/resolver-owned roots are also not settable: blob_ref, blobs, source_authoring. Bind sources with set_source_from_blob or set_source_from_blobs instead. When field_path targets an LLM node, its runtime-owned top-level option is also not settable: approved_prompt_artifact_hash. For author-owned LLM option edits use patch_node_options, or upsert_node for a full node edit; blob wiring cannot author those values.'}, 'blob_id': {'type': 'string', 'format': 'uuid', 'description': 'Ready blob ID to wire as inline content.'}, 'encoding': {'type': 'string', 'enum': ['latin-1', 'utf-16', 'utf-8', 'utf-8-sig'], 'default': 'utf-8', 'description': 'Text decoder used at runtime. Defaults to utf-8.'}}, 'required': ['field_path', 'blob_id'], 'additionalProperties': False}}}, {'type': 'function', 'function': {'name': 'list_sources', 'description': "List available source plugins. Each entry carries its full `config_fields` (name, type, required, description, default per option), usage guidance, `composer_hints`, and `secret_requirements` — not just a name and blurb. The result's `prohibited` array names any source categorically banned from the web authoring surface by security policy, with its closed reason and explanation — cite it when a user asks why a specific plugin is unavailable. Call get_plugin_schema on