ess, on_error, input, routes, and fork_to are siblings of options; edit them with upsert_edge or upsert_node. For a gate, edit on_error only with upsert_node. If prompt_template_parts exists, edit that structure while preserving interpretation_ref entries; do not change only the compiled prompt_template. A patched schema declares arriving types for consumed fields and output types for created fields. To convert an arriving value, change the source contract (patch_source_options) or insert a type_coerce upstream; a declaration does not convert. Runtime-owned LLM option fields are not settable: approved_prompt_artifact_hash. Omit them; ELSPETH re-derives them during review reconciliation or execution. Inside interpretation_requirements, only kind, user_term, and draft, with optional display_title (a non-empty string of at most 200 characters) are authorable. display_title is a concise human-readable approval name. Resolver-owned fields are not settable: accepted_artifact_hash, accepted_value, event_id, id, resolved_prompt_template_hash, status. Omit those fields. On incremental surfaces, persist an authorable pending review with the offered mutation tool and call request_interpretation_review when offered. On a proposal-only surface, include the pending requirements in the appropriate source/node options of the complete proposal instead. Backend-owned review kinds are surfaced automatically. The user resolves the card and ELSPETH writes resolved review metadata.'}}, 'required': ['node_id', 'patch'], 'additionalProperties': False}, 'strict': None, 'type': 'function', 'description': "Apply a shallow merge-patch to a node's options. Use this for option-only edits. Keys in the patch overwrite existing keys. Keys set to null are deleted. Missing keys are unchanged. For an existing structured LLM prompt, edit prompt_template_parts and preserve interpretation_ref entries; prompt_template is compiled from those parts. Changed prompt context requires fresh review. Do not use this for node routing fields such as on_success/on_error/input/routes; use upsert_edge or upsert_node for routing edits. Gate on_error is node-level and must use upsert_node."}, {'name': 'set_output', 'parameters': {'type': 'object', 'properties': {'sink_name': {'type': 'string', 'description': "Sink name: BOTH the sink's identifier (used by patch_output_options/remove_output) AND the connection-name the sink consumes — it MUST equal some upstream's on_success value; it need not match any node id."}, 'plugin': {'type': 'string', 'description': "Sink plugin name (e.g. 'csv', 'json')."}, 'options': {'type': 'object', 'description': 'Plugin-specific config. For csv/document/json/text file sinks in runnable web pipelines, include path, schema, and explicit collision_policy. Sink schema.fields and custom header keys use the carried row names, normally normalized source headers or mapping targets. The interpretation_requirements option root is not settable on outputs. Stage an authorable review on its source or node instead.'}, 'on_write_failure': {'type': ['string', 'null'], 'description': "Explicit non-empty write-failure choice required for new sinks: 'discard' records the drop; an eligible sink name diverts failed rows. Omit only to preserve this existing sink's choice. Null/empty is invalid."}, 'description': {'type': ['string', 'null'], 'description': 'One short sentence of plain prose saying what this step does, shown to reviewers on the Spec tab. Supply it when creating the step and refresh it whenever you change what the step does. Informational only — never affects validation or execution.'}}, 'required': ['sink_name', 'plugin', 'options'], 'additionalProperties': False}, 'strict': None, 'type': 'function', 'description': 'Add or replace a pipeline output (sink).'}, {'name': 'remove_output', 'parameters': {'type': 'object', 'properties': {'sink_name': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Sink name to remove.'}}, 'required': ['sink_name'], 'additionalProperties': False}, 'strict': None, 'type': 'function', 'description': 'Remove a pipeline output (sink) by name.'}, {'name': 'patch_output_options', 'parameters': {'type': 'object', 'properties': {'sink_name': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Name of the output (sink) to patch.'}, 'patch': {'type': 'object', 'description': 'Merge-patch to apply to output options. The interpretation_requirements option root is not settable on outputs. Stage an authorable review on its source or node instead.'}}, 'required': ['sink_name', 'patch'], 'additionalProperties': False}, 'strict': None, 'type': 'function', 'description': "Apply a shallow merge-patch to an output's options. Keys in the patch overwrite existing keys. Keys set to null are deleted. Missing keys are unchanged."}, {'name': 'list_secret_refs', 'parameters': {'type': 'object', 'properties': {}, 'required': [], 'additionalProperties': False}, 'strict': None, 'type': 'function', 'description': 'List available secret references (API keys, credentials). Each entry carries the reference `name`, its `scope`, `source_kind`, `available` (true when it resolves for you), and `reason` (why not, when it does not); never values.'}, {'name': 'validate_secret_ref', 'parameters': {'type': 'object', 'properties': {'name': {'type': 'string', 'description': "Secret reference name (e.g. 'OPENROUTER_API_KEY')."}}, 'required': ['name'], 'additionalProperties': False}, 'strict': None, 'type': 'function', 'description': 'Check if a secret reference exists and is accessible to the current user. Returns the checked reference `name` and `available` (true when it resolves for you). When the reference appears in your inventory, also returns its `scope`, `source_kind`, and `reason` (null when available; otherwise the reason it cannot resolve).'}, {'name': 'request_advisor_hint', 'parameters': {'type': 'object', 'properties': {'trigger': {'type': 'string', 'enum': ['proactive_security_safety', 'proactive_red_listed_plugin', 'cannot_complete'], 'description': 'Why this advisor call is allowed. Use cannot_complete for an early-return review of a specific suspected blocker, without requiring a formal impossibility proof. Use proactive_security_safety before set_pipeline for security/safety-sensitive flows. Use proactive_red_listed_plugin before set_pipeline when the plan uses a red-listed plugin such as llm, database, dataverse, Azure safety transforms, RAG retrieval, or Chroma sinks.'}, 'problem_summary': {'type': 'string', 'maxLength': 2000, 'description': "Your own statement of what you are trying to do and why you are stuck, with secrets and PII removed. One or two sentences. Be specific: 'I cannot get llm transform options to validate against the Azure provider schema' is useful; 'help' is not."}, 'recent_errors': {'type': 'array', 'maxItems': 5, 'items': {'type': 'string', 'maxLength': 2000}, 'description': 'Redacted summaries of the last validator errors, most recent first. Include up to 5; remove secrets and PII.'}, 'attempted_actions': {'type': 'array', 'maxItems': 8, 'items': {'type': 'string', 'maxLength': 2000}, 'description': 'What you have already tried, one item per attempt. Include the tool name and a one-line summary of the argument shape. The advisor uses this to avoid suggesting things you have already ruled out.'}, 'schema_excerpt': {'type': 'string', 'maxLength': 8000, 'description': 'Optional — the relevant, redacted plugin schema snippet you are working against, as returned by `get_plugin_schema`. Including this lets the advisor give field-level guidance grounded in the exact contract.'}}, 'required': ['trigger', 'problem_summary', 'recent_errors', 'attempted_actions'], 'additionalProperties': False}, 'strict': None, 'type': 'function', 'description': 'ESCAPE HATCH — use cannot_complete as soon as missing or contradictory information, an unavailable capability, or an unreasonable requirement prevents a faithful result. Give your specific reason, evidence and attempted actions. Call it ALONE in its ba