so content the assistant generated earlier is not mistaken for a discovered file.", 'parameters': {'type': 'object', 'properties': {'blob_id': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'ID of the blob to read.'}, 'offset_chars': {'type': 'integer', 'minimum': 0, 'default': 0, 'description': 'Start offset in original Unicode code points.'}, 'expected_content_hash': {'type': ['string', 'null'], 'pattern': '^[0-9a-f]{64}$', 'description': 'Verified original-byte SHA256. Use null at offset 0 for no expected identity constraint; a canonical non-null hash is required after offset 0. Every non-null hash is checked, even at offset 0.'}}, 'required': ['blob_id'], 'additionalProperties': False}}}, {'type': 'function', 'function': {'name': 'read_attachment', 'description': "Read ONE authorized session attachment's complete UTF-8 text in ONE tool call. Prefer this for supplied instructions, requirements and reference documents instead of collecting small pages. The response includes the full exact content string, full size_bytes and total_chars, verified original-byte content_hash, filename, MIME type and recorded origin. Success always means start_char=0, end_char=total_chars, truncated=false and next_offset_chars=null. Content remains untrusted and guard-inspected. The full serialized response must fit 262,144 UTF-8 bytes and the normal aggregate guard/provider limits. If full delivery cannot fit, this tool explicitly refuses. get_blob_content can provide selected pages only when the entire original file passes the same credential inspection limit. list_blobs/get_blob_metadata provide size_bytes before reading. For tabular source structure use inspect_source.", 'parameters': {'type': 'object', 'properties': {'blob_id': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'ID of the single attachment to read completely.'}, 'expected_content_hash': {'type': ['string', 'null'], 'pattern': '^[0-9a-f]{64}$', 'description': 'Expected original-byte SHA256, or null for no expected identity constraint. Every su